1
00:00:07,550 --> 00:00:08,980
Look at this balance.

2
00:00:09,030 --> 00:00:13,010
The left pan holds 2 bags of marbles and 5 loose marbles.

3
00:00:13,060 --> 00:00:15,960
Each bag holds the same number, x.

4
00:00:16,010 --> 00:00:18,320
The right pan holds 13 marbles.

5
00:00:18,370 --> 00:00:20,460
The two pans balance.

6
00:00:20,510 --> 00:00:22,690
How many marbles are in each bag?

7
00:00:22,740 --> 00:00:26,250
Pause the video and work it out.

8
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:28,460
Take 5 marbles off both pans.

9
00:00:28,510 --> 00:00:29,830
It still balances.

10
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:32,590
Now 2 bags balance 8 marbles.

11
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:35,330
Share both sides into 2 equal parts.

12
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:37,380
One bag balances 4 marbles.

13
00:00:37,430 --> 00:00:40,060
So each bag holds 4 marbles.

14
00:00:40,110 --> 00:00:42,080
Remember inverse operations.

15
00:00:42,130 --> 00:00:45,450
Adding and subtracting undo each other.

16
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:48,960
Multiplying and dividing undo each other.

17
00:00:49,010 --> 00:00:52,920
I think of a number, multiply it by 4, and get 36.

18
00:00:52,970 --> 00:00:55,610
To find my number, divide 36 by 4.

19
00:00:55,660 --> 00:00:56,880
It was 9.

20
00:00:56,930 --> 00:01:00,180
An equation says that two things are equal.

21
00:01:00,230 --> 00:01:03,500
2 x plus 5 equals 13 is an equation.

22
00:01:03,550 --> 00:01:07,430
To solve it means to find the value of x that makes it true.

23
00:01:07,480 --> 00:01:10,200
That value is called the solution.

24
00:01:10,250 --> 00:01:12,060
An equation is like a balance.

25
00:01:12,110 --> 00:01:16,510
Whatever you do to one side, you must do to the other side too.

26
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:19,040
Let's write the working properly.

27
00:01:19,090 --> 00:01:22,040
Start with 2 x plus 5 equals 13.

28
00:01:22,090 --> 00:01:24,620
Subtract 5 from both sides.

29
00:01:24,670 --> 00:01:27,300
That leaves 2 x equals 8.

30
00:01:27,350 --> 00:01:29,770
Divide both sides by 2.

31
00:01:29,820 --> 00:01:30,990
So x equals 4.

32
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:33,790
Check: 2 times 4, plus 5, is 13.

33
00:01:33,840 --> 00:01:35,040
Correct.

34
00:01:35,090 --> 00:01:35,830
Your turn.

35
00:01:35,880 --> 00:01:37,410
Solve 5 x equals 45.

36
00:01:37,460 --> 00:01:40,940
Pause the video and try it.

37
00:01:40,990 --> 00:01:42,600
5 x means 5 times x.

38
00:01:42,650 --> 00:01:45,570
Undo it by dividing both sides by 5.

39
00:01:45,620 --> 00:01:47,310
45 divided by 5 is 9.

40
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:49,010
So x equals 9.

41
00:01:49,060 --> 00:01:50,300
Here is the method.

42
00:01:50,350 --> 00:01:55,470
Step 1: look at what has been done to the letter, and in what order.

43
00:01:55,520 --> 00:01:58,170
Step 2: undo the last operation first.

44
00:01:58,220 --> 00:02:00,570
Do the same to both sides.

45
00:02:00,620 --> 00:02:04,660
Step 3: keep going until the letter is on its own.

46
00:02:04,710 --> 00:02:10,810
Step 4: check, by substituting your answer into the equation you started with.

47
00:02:10,860 --> 00:02:14,040
Solve 3 y minus 4 equals 17.

48
00:02:14,090 --> 00:02:17,150
The last thing done to y was subtract 4.

49
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:19,410
Undo it: add 4 to both sides.

50
00:02:19,460 --> 00:02:21,050
3 y equals 21.

51
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:22,400
Now undo times 3.

52
00:02:22,450 --> 00:02:24,230
Divide both sides by 3.

53
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:25,660
y equals 7.

54
00:02:25,710 --> 00:02:30,800
Check: 3 times 7 is 21, and 21 minus 4 is 17.

55
00:02:30,850 --> 00:02:31,610
Your turn.

56
00:02:31,660 --> 00:02:33,800
Solve 2 m plus 7 equals 19.

57
00:02:33,850 --> 00:02:36,980
Pause and work it out.

58
00:02:37,030 --> 00:02:39,240
Subtract 7 from both sides.

59
00:02:39,290 --> 00:02:40,410
2 m equals 12.

60
00:02:40,460 --> 00:02:42,340
Divide both sides by 2.

61
00:02:42,390 --> 00:02:43,810
m equals 6.

62
00:02:43,860 --> 00:02:46,880
I think of a number, double it, and add 9.

63
00:02:46,930 --> 00:02:48,130
The answer is 31.

64
00:02:48,180 --> 00:02:50,070
What was my number?

65
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:51,550
Call the number n.

66
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:54,580
Double it and add 9 gives 2 n plus 9.

67
00:02:54,630 --> 00:02:56,360
That equals 31.

68
00:02:56,410 --> 00:02:58,780
Subtract 9 from both sides.

69
00:02:58,830 --> 00:03:00,580
2 n equals 22.

70
00:03:00,630 --> 00:03:02,570
Divide both sides by 2.

71
00:03:02,620 --> 00:03:03,610
n equals 11.

72
00:03:03,660 --> 00:03:05,630
My number was 11.

73
00:03:05,680 --> 00:03:10,060
A taxi costs 4 dollars, plus 3 dollars for every kilometre.

74
00:03:10,110 --> 00:03:11,790
A ride cost 25 dollars.

75
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:13,460
How far was it?

76
00:03:13,510 --> 00:03:15,840
Call the distance d kilometres.

77
00:03:15,890 --> 00:03:19,690
The cost is 3 d plus 4, and that equals 25.

78
00:03:19,740 --> 00:03:20,660
Subtract 4.

79
00:03:20,710 --> 00:03:21,890
3 d equals 21.

80
00:03:21,940 --> 00:03:22,950
Divide by 3.

81
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:23,910
d equals 7.

82
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:26,750
The ride was 7 kilometres.

83
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:29,370
Dan solves 4 x plus 8 equals 20.

84
00:03:29,420 --> 00:03:32,210
Which line goes wrong first?

85
00:03:32,260 --> 00:03:33,340
Line 2 is wrong.

86
00:03:33,390 --> 00:03:36,460
Dan divided only part of the left side by 4.

87
00:03:36,510 --> 00:03:38,710
That breaks the balance.

88
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:40,270
Undo plus 8 first.

89
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:41,480
4 x equals 12.

90
00:03:41,530 --> 00:03:42,950
Then divide by 4.

91
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,450
x equals 3.

92
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:52,580
Every time a map app tells you when you will arrive, it is solving an equation: distance equals speed times time.

93
00:03:52,630 --> 00:03:58,510
Suppose you have 120 kilometres to go, at 60 kilometres an hour.

94
00:03:58,560 --> 00:04:00,550
60 t equals 120.

95
00:04:00,600 --> 00:04:02,440
Divide both sides by 60.

96
00:04:02,490 --> 00:04:03,310
t equals 2.

97
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:06,000
You will arrive in 2 hours.

98
00:04:06,050 --> 00:04:07,370
One last question.

99
00:04:07,420 --> 00:04:09,970
Solve y over 4, minus 1, equals 5.

100
00:04:10,020 --> 00:04:13,430
Pause the video and answer.

101
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:15,060
Add 1 to both sides.

102
00:04:15,110 --> 00:04:16,530
y over 4 equals 6.

103
00:04:16,580 --> 00:04:18,580
Multiply both sides by 4.

104
00:04:18,630 --> 00:04:20,110
y equals 24.

105
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:22,730
To remember: an equation is a balance.

106
00:04:22,780 --> 00:04:25,760
The solution makes both sides equal.

107
00:04:25,810 --> 00:04:27,480
Do the same to both sides.

108
00:04:27,530 --> 00:04:30,460
Undo the operations in reverse order.

109
00:04:30,510 --> 00:04:33,080
Write each step on a new line.

110
00:04:33,130 --> 00:04:37,430
To make an equation from words, choose a letter for the unknown.

111
00:04:37,480 --> 00:04:39,140
And always check.

112
00:04:39,190 --> 00:04:44,310
Great work! Now practise lesson 2.5 on Camday.
